meta {
  name: Current session
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/get-session
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Origin: {{webOrigin}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  Reads the session from the cookie and returns the user and their session. It
  is how the web app finds out who is logged in when a page loads: the token
  lives in an `httpOnly` cookie that JavaScript cannot read, so calling this
  route is the only way.

  **Responses you will see**

  | Status | When |
  | --- | --- |
  | 200 with a body | Valid cookie |
  | 200 with body `null` | No cookie, or an expired session — not an error |

  With no session it answers 200 with `null`, not 401: it is a Better Auth
  route, not a product route. It goes through neither the `AuthGuard` nor the
  `AllExceptionsFilter`, so its error body does not follow the rest of the
  API's `{"error": "..."}` either.

  The session lasts 90 days and renews after each day of use — check the
  `Max-Age` of the `Set-Cookie` in the sign-up's Headers tab: 7776000 seconds.
}
